---A compliance violation that's detected by Assured Workloads monitoring. A violation is created when an organization policy or a resource in a workload (or a Data Boundary scope) changes in a way that doesn't comply with the controls of the applicable compliance regime or framework.
---@class gcp.unstable.assuredworkloads_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAssuredworkloadsV1beta1Violation
---@field description? string Output only. A description of the violation. For example, `OrgPolicy gcp.resourceLocations has non compliant value.`
---@field category? string Output only. The category that the violation is mapped to. For example, `Location`, `Service Usage`, `Access`, or `Encryption`.
---@field violationType? gcp.unstable.assuredworkloads_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAssuredworkloadsV1beta1ViolationViolationTypeEnum Output only. The type of the violation.
---@field exceptionContexts? gcp.unstable.assuredworkloads_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAssuredworkloadsV1beta1ViolationExceptionContextList Output only. The details of all of the acknowledgements (exceptions) for the violation.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time when the violation record was last updated.
---@field exceptionAuditLogLink? string Output only. Immutable. A link to the Cloud Audit Logs entries that contain the business justification that was provided when the violation was acknowledged. Format: `https://console.cloud.google.com/logs/query;query={logName}{protoPayload.resourceName}{protoPayload.methodName}{timeRange}{organization}`
---@field nonCompliantOrgPolicy? string Output only. Immutable. The name of the organization policy that was modified with a non-compliant change and resulted in this violation. Formats: * `projects/{project_number}/policies/{constraint_name}` * `folders/{folder_id}/policies/{constraint_name}` * `organizations/{organization_id}/policies/{constraint_name}`
---@field name? string Output only. Immutable. The resource name of the violation. Format: `organizations/{organization}/locations/{location}/workloads/{workload_id}/violations/{violations_id}`
---@field state? gcp.unstable.assuredworkloads_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAssuredworkloadsV1beta1ViolationStateEnum Output only. The state of the violation.
---@field remediation? gcp.unstable.assuredworkloads_v1beta1.GoogleCloudAssuredworkloadsV1beta1ViolationRemediation Output only. The remediation guidance for the violation.
---@field acknowledgementTime? string Optional. The time when the violation was first acknowledged. To find the most recent time that the violation was acknowledged, check `exception_contexts`. This field is absent when `acknowledged` is `false`.
---@field resourceType? string Optional. Output only. For resource violations, the type of the non-compliant resource. For example, `compute.googleapis.com/Disk`. This field is empty for organization policy violations.
---@field beginTime? string Output only. The time of the event that triggered the violation.
---@field parentProjectNumber? string Optional. Output only. For resource violations, the number of the project that contains the non-compliant resource. This field is empty for organization policy violations.
---@field resourceName? string Optional. Output only. For resource violations, the full resource name of the non-compliant resource. For example, `//storage.googleapis.com/myprojectxyz-testbucket`. This field is empty for organization policy violations.
---@field acknowledged? boolean Whether the violation has been acknowledged.
---@field associatedOrgPolicyViolationId? string Optional. Output only. For resource violations, the ID of the organization policy violation that caused this resource violation. This field is empty for organization policy violations.
---@field resolveTime? string Output only. The time of the event that resolved the violation. This field is empty if the violation is unresolved.
---@field remediationMarkdown? string Output only. The remediation instructions for the violation, in Markdown format. This field is only populated by `GetViolation` when using `VIOLATION_VIEW_DATA_BOUNDARY`. When this field isn't populated, see `remediation` instead.
---@field auditLogLink? string Output only. Immutable. A link to the Cloud Audit Logs entries for the violated resource. Format: `https://console.cloud.google.com/logs/query;query={logName}{protoPayload.resourceName}{timeRange}{folder}`
---@field affectedFrameworks? gcp.unstable.assuredworkloads_v1beta1.StringList Output only. The IDs of the compliance frameworks that are affected by this violation. For example, `builtin-fedramp-high`. This field is only populated when using `VIOLATION_VIEW_DATA_BOUNDARY`.
---@field orgPolicyConstraint? string Output only. Immutable. Deprecated: This field is deprecated and might be removed in a future version of the API. Use `non_compliant_org_policy` instead, which contains the full resource name of the organization policy, including the constraint name. The organization policy constraint that was changed in a non-compliant way, which resulted in this violation.
---@field childResourceViolationCount? number Optional. Output only. For organization policy violations, the number of resource violations that are associated with this violation. This field is `0` for resource violations.

