---@field pageToken? string Optional. A page token, received from a previous `ListViolations` call. Provide this token to retrieve the subsequent page. When paginating, all other parameters that are provided to `ListViolations` must match the call that provided the page token.
---@field ["interval.endTime"]? string The end of the time window.
---@field pageSize? number Optional. The maximum number of violations to return. The service might return fewer violations than this value. If unspecified, at most 100 violations are returned. The maximum value is 1000; values above 1000 are coerced to 1000.
---@field filter? string Optional. A filter expression that restricts the violations that are returned. The syntax follows [AIP-160](https://google.aip.dev/160). Only the equality operator (`=`) is supported, and expressions can be combined with `AND`, `OR`, and `NOT`. When `view` is `VIOLATION_VIEW_DATA_BOUNDARY`, the following fields are supported: `violationId`, `category`, `state` (`UNRESOLVED`, `RESOLVED`, or `EXCEPTION`), `violationType` (`ORG_POLICY` or `RESOURCE`), `resourceType`, `resourceName`, `project`, `associatedOrgPolicyViolationId`, `cloudControlName`, `workloadDisplayName`, and `complianceType` (a framework ID). Example: `state = "UNRESOLVED" AND complianceType = "builtin-fedramp-high"`
